 * has an INCOMPLETE header set on this cluster: its include/json-c/ is missing
 * json_object_iterator.h, which json-c/json.h #includes unconditionally. That breaks
 * ANY recompile of a file that includes json.h (e.g. src/tools/fscanreal.c). The
 * iterator API is stable and unchanged from json-c 0.10 through 0.17, and the exported
 * symbols (json_object_iter_*) ARE present in libjson-c.so.4, so this faithful
 * reconstruction of the 0.13.1 header is ABI-compatible.
 *
 * It reuses <json-c/json_object.h> for JSON_EXPORT / json_bool / struct json_object
 * (all defined there in 0.13.1), instead of the 0.17-only json_types.h split.
 *
 * Put on the include path via CPATH at build time; touches no system files.
